# The product's real browser support target. eslint-plugin-compat checks web APIs against this.
# Replace `defaults` with the product's actual targets, but KEEP `not op_mini all`:
# Opera Mini is a proxy browser that supports almost no modern API (fetch, Promise.all,
# structuredClone), so leaving it in makes the compat gate false-positive on completely normal
# code. Proven 2026-06-25: a real product flagged 20 false "fetch not supported in op_mini all"
# errors with a bare `defaults`; adding `not op_mini all` dropped them to zero with no real gap lost.
#
# IMPORTANT - use EXACTLY ONE browserslist source. If the product ALREADY has a `browserslist` key in
# package.json (most frontend products do), do NOT also add this file: browserslist THROWS "contains
# both .browserslistrc and package.json with browserslist" and the compat gate breaks (verified
# 2026-06-25). In that case, add `not op_mini all` to the existing package.json list instead.
defaults
not op_mini all
not dead
